P3, bench/harbor/hill.ts:136 with bench/harbor/analysis/round-score.ts:116,132: `leader` is now set whenever `publishedLeader` returns a name. The old code dropped the leader when that harness had no full-stage cell (`leaderCell === undefined`), and the new code no longer checks this. If the published leader has no public full-stage cell at that model and effort, no row is marked "(published leader)", but the explanation line still prints. Whether this can happen depends on what `publishedLeader` returns, which I did not check, so the issue is UNVERIFIED. Fix: set `leader` only when `field.some(f => f.harness === leader)`. That also makes the `leader` field mean "the marked row".

The docs (METHODOLOGY.md:12,152-156,217 and README.md:177,190) match the new output. The test change checks the per-harness paired difference with values that can fail. Removing the exports of `setupKey` and `BoardSetup` is safe, because round-score.ts no longer imports `setupKey`.",
